00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.240
I feel like they're pretty relevant today as well.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.480
And just to confirm, for you, Mike, he did direct Sudden Impact.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.280
Yeah, that's what I'm saying. That that's the only one of the five.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:19.320
Yeah. Right, right, right. So that was part of my, like, I had my Blu-ray collection of Clint Eastwood directorial things because it was on sale for like 80% off.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:24.140
And I was like, sure, I don't know if I want to watch Invictus, but I'll watch some of this stuff.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.840
You don't have to justify why you bought this.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:31.760
Invictus. Okay. There was way worse stuff on there than Invictus for what it's worth.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.020
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.440
But I'm actually surprised.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.580
And I, you know, I remember it being a reference in Zodiac.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.160
But I don't remember this being about the Zodiac killer.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:52.680
Like, this is just some kind of, like, you know, after you've seen Zodiac, everything feels kind of like cartoony after the fact.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:07:04.260
But it's basically the same setup, except from the police point of view, of the, you know, the 2007 David Fincher classic.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.560
Yeah, yeah, that's true.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.940
Because it's even referenced in the film, right?

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.940
Like, he's at the movie theater or something in Zodiac?

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:16.020
Yeah, they go, yeah, they end up seeing, oh, they're already making movies about it.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:26.380
Like, yeah. Right. Another funny thing about this movie, which, by the way, even though the movie, the first movie is called Dirty Harry and the game is called Dirty Harry, they don't share a plot.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.620
No, nothing about it in the game.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:31.480
Yeah, nothing about them. They just both, obviously, lean on the iconic character.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:42.120
The movie also has, like, a small Mandela effect, where, like, that quote of the do you feel lucky punk, that's not what he says.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.320
It's do I feel lucky?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.120
But he's not talking about himself.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.180
Yeah, you've got to ask yourself, right?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.420
So it's like, do you feel lucky is, like, a good way to, like, re-say the quote.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:59.060
Yeah. Right. Because do I feel lucky sounds like Clint's a gambling man.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:00.380
Well, I mean, I think.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:01.920
Whereas he's really challenging the gambling.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:08.420
They're really just, in this movie, just referencing the Google search option.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.340
So, I mean, however you say it, it's basically just.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.640
Feeling lucky. Yeah.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.320
You're just sort of, it's a remix of a remix.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.140
Sean, that is a great idea.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:25.880
You know, Google always does, like, fun web pages for anniversaries or specific dates and stuff.

