00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:21.480
So, I agree, especially because they're leaning into, you know, like, that line about the, you know, do you feel lucky, punk, and all that.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.020
It makes sense. They say it pretty often.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.180
Right, right. It makes sense.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.580
But here's the thing, just to go back to the beginning of the game.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.420
I don't want to recap everything I said, but there is some kind of cardinal sin about, like, a level starting immediately.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.920
Like, that's a jank feeling of, like, why am I just being, like, thrown into something that feels like it was already happening?

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:44.800
But why are, like, two enemies literally punching you at the start?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.360
Like, are you waking up from something?

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.320
Are you waking up from the previous game over?

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:54.580
Yeah, it's just, like, this is where, no, this is just, like, where you pick up the story.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.240
But, like, moments before was, like, exactly the same part of the story.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.560
They're just like, yeah, we'll start you here.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:07.420
Right, right. You could have just started a couple frames over to the left and just started beating them up instead, but they chose you to be in the middle of them.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:20.280
Yeah, if this was a more modern game, maybe it would start with a cutscene of, like, I don't know, something completely unrelated to Dirty Harry because he never got himself into these situations, like, all willy-nilly.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:23.580
It really is strange.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:35.940
Like, you'd think that, like, if you wanted to at least even add to the fact that maybe this is the character that you remember from in the movies, maybe just have him leave a police station and walk out onto the street.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:44.120
Or is it really that important to immediately say to everyone, like, no, this is an action game.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.660
You're going to have to be really good at this.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.080
I don't know. It felt like a very strange decision.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.980
I agree. Getting around in the city, sometimes it's like, where the hell do I go?

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:59.020
But it's because streets are not simple left to right side-scrolling levels.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:06.200
You can not only walk throughout the streets, but you can walk into alleys or through doors to side areas.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.140
You can go down into the sewers via the manholes.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.600
It's easy. You can climb power lines.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:19.760
Right. It's easy to kind of get, like, lost in this larger, like, what's my objective?

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:27.180
You know, like, you're kind of just exploring, but you don't have, like, a quest thing to be like, well, first you should go into this building and do this.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.300
Then you should go into this alleyway.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.640
You kind of just have to figure it all out.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:45.040
So while it is a pretty impressive city to walk around in for NES days, like, compared to, I guess, like, we've had some other ones where it's more, like, top down and you're driving around in a city and then you go to levels.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:59.220
This feels okay, but it's the controls that make it so tough to get around that really, like, limit the amount of exploration you want to do before you're just like, okay, where the hell do I go?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:05.560
Yeah. What's impressive to me about it on paper is that it's not that top down style where you're used to sitting in other games.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:06.760
And it is a side scroller.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.740
It's like a beat them up side scroller, like any other one that we've played.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:13.320
But you can go into a bunch of the buildings and you can go into all the buildings.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.380
You hear that GTA?

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:21.960
But, like, you can go into all the buildings and you can, like, there is a city, but it's in a side scrolling style.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.440
And that is a really cool, like, design idea for me.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.520
And I love that idea for games.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:38.280
I just don't know if, like, each of the parts of this work together or, like, if it just gets kind of frustrating, actually, in practice.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.180
Or maybe it's just the way this game pulled it off.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.460
The controls really are a mystery.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.020
And I think this, I'm going to answer this in two parts.

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:56.120
I think that the bigger sin here is, at least specifically in this level, is the lack of direction.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:02.360
Because this is kind of, like, a, it's a huge riddle.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.060
You're supposed to, like, progress in this game.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.940
Like, are you supposed to go in the sewers?

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:12.140
Is that, like, the end goal is to get to the bottom of the sewers?

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:17.160
Or is there, like, a, or is there, like, a building you're supposed to gain access to?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:23.980
You end up figuring out that, yes, it's the sewers because you've pressed every other option.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:29.400
And I guess, like, the main progression point there is to get, like, a flashlight.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:39.960
But, yeah, the controls are so strange, though, that I would say that, I know that, Mike, I know you don't like up as jump.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:42.540
I'm okay with up as jump.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:48.620
But even you, I think, can agree that up is better as jump than A and B.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.800
A hundred percent. Yes.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:55.540
You know what? I'm going to play Crazy Devil's Advocate here.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:59.500
I would have agreed with you when I read the manual of this and I saw A and B was jump.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.720
But in practice, in this game, I think I like it better than up.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.300
I don't think it's great, but I think up is just more annoying because I can't keep moving forward.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.980
Like, it's just not as fluid to me.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.220
Okay, Joe, then.

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:13.320
But let me just, let me press you there, though.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:19.480
Okay. Let's say that, like, okay, A and B is jump and you're okay with that.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:23.400
Now, do you think maybe up should be how you interact with people?

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:32.760
Or should it be you jump like a weirdo in front of them and that's how you get any kind of, like, pickup from that person?

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:47.540
Because there's nothing weirder to me than, like, finding that room with the girl that gives you the extra lives past, like, the big dude that's bulletproof than having to, like, jump clear over her head and then land again.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.740
And that's how you, like, get the lives.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:50.760
It's so goofy.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.320
I mean, I don't feel like that's pressing me.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:19:04.800
I mean, I think that those can be, those are not, like, those are, like, very exclusive two different things where, like, I think A and B is better than up for me, but also what you just described is really stupid and I hate it.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:10.900
So, like, I don't want both of those things to be true, but, like, I don't think A and B is ideal.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:14.060
But I just, it just didn't bother me as much as I thought when I read it in the manual.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.220
I was like, well, that's going to be awful.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.500
And then I kind of forgot about it.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:17.520
I got used to it pretty quickly.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:23.500
And even if the control isn't bad, we can agree that the jump itself is just bad.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.780
It's just a bad jump.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:25.840
It's very stiff.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.880
Yeah. He's quite, he can gallop, though.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.160
He's a good jumper.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.500
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. Great, great jumper from no momentum.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.240
And I assume he does a lot of acrobatics in the movie and stuff and he climbs and jumps.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:41.100
He does jump from a bridge onto a bus in the first movie.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.860
Oh, okay. Then you've got to be a good jumper for that.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.100
So that might be based on the movie.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.220
We were talking about getting around in the city.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.900
And, you know, I guess in one way they're trying to encourage exploration.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:58.620
But they're really not because that door closes as soon as you enter the ha ha ha room.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.720
Did you guys come across this?

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.620
I heard about it.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.660
Yeah. Thankfully, I didn't come across it.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:12.940
Okay. So this room, when you enter it from the door, you're just in a room where the letters ha ha ha are on the wall.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.920
And you're soft locked.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.380
You have to reset the game.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.820
Yeah. Can I do my essential games vote right now, actually?

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:22.100
How the hell did he get in that room?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.420
There's no more door?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.540
Like, what happened?

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.360
Yeah. It's a one-time use.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.200
There's nothing off screen, you know?

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.380
Like, if it's on screen, it says exit.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.460
And in real life, things will say exit in a place that you can see it.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.360
I don't know. Fourth wall joke.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:40.660
I don't understand.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:45.620
Yeah, fourth wall joke that makes you have to reset your game and just start over.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.800
No, it's bad. It's very bad.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.280
I don't know what they were thinking.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:55.040
Why they think that this would be an acceptable way to treat the player.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:57.480
Like, it's actually insulting.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.620
And it's, like, far into that first level, too.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.800
It's not like...

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.120
Like, if you got there, you made some progress that you lost there.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.040
I should go back to the jump, though, because the jump is important for two other things.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:14.320
Jumping on snakes is how you kill them, just like in real life.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:17.380
That's true. If you want to take care of a snake, just jump on it.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.580
You jump on boxes, you jump on snakes.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.740
Jumping is also how you change clothes.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:25.700
Yep. Jump. You have to jump on the guy with the white clothes.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:26.960
Specifically in front of Michael Jackson.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:32.620
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You jump on the guy with the white clothes, Michael Jackson, and then you become Michael Jackson as a result.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:36.940
But it's also, like, how you interact with other people in the game, too.

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.100
Like, you just jump in front of them, and there's that woman.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:41.920
Yeah, the girl in the red dress.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.680
That's how you get lives, I guess.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:22:03.100
Which I'll also, this is, every time you pick up an item by either jumping on a box or kicking a piece of furniture, which, again, I don't remember from the movie as being his main interaction with the environment, but it will just give you the briefest flash of the thing that you supposedly picked up.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.940
You're supposed to kind of just understand.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.280
Like, sometimes you'll know, oh, that was a crowbar, but then there's just other shapes.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:15.480
I don't know. Yeah, and there's, like, there aren't all bad ideas.

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:23.100
Like, I feel like we're talking a lot about the funny things, but, like, there was that interesting bodyguard thing, even though they won't tell you in the game what you need to do.

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:35.060
He's, like, the bouncer who will attack you, and you can't attack him if you're trying to get through the door until you change suits, and then it's like, oh, right this way, come through.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.080
I'm not saying that's genius, right?

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:46.140
But, like, that is at least, like, they have the idea of gating progress besides just being, like, the door's locked.

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:50.960
Go find the key. I did not realize that it was my clothes that made that happen.

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:55.300
I thought that I just, I thought I jumped past him in the right way.

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:01.560
But I guess I had the suit on at that point, and I just, I tricked myself.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:06.960
Before we move on, one other thing about just the controls and Harry.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:11.260
So, he's able to draw the gun, but not shoot it.

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:13.500
And that, we talked about how that looks cool and all.

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:25.620
Shouldn't he have been able to, like, shouldn't there have been, like, something where he can threaten, or the enemies could feel threatened by just him drawing the gun and kind of, like, nope out of the situation?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.240
Like, wouldn't that have been interesting?

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.480
That would have been more Dirty Harry.

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:30.720
Dirty Harry? Right, you know?

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.960
Like, he's more, like, in your face.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:34.800
Like, is this guy really going to shoot me?

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:35.720
He's a cop.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.880
He shouldn't shoot me, but he looks kind of crazy.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:38.720
Maybe he will.

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:40.320
But they don't give a shit.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:41.960
Like, they're just, like, coming at you.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:49.220
Yeah, I mean, was this game, I mean, not to get ahead of whatever, like, developer notes, but was this game designed to be a Dirty Harry game?

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:52.100
Or was this just a game that didn't have anything to do with Dirty Harry?

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:54.380
I think that it definitely was.

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:55.800
It had to have been.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:59.000
There's too many, like, just Clint Eastwood references and everything.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.420
Well, yeah, but I mean, like, originally, like, you know, they just slapped that stuff in at the end after they were like, all right, yeah, let's just make it Clint Eastwood.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:11.500
Let's make it. To the best of my knowledge, this was always a Dirty Harry game.

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:13.520
Well, then, weird decisions.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:20.460
Yeah. Weird decisions all around because, keep in mind, the Dirty Harry series ended in 1988.

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:27.460
So it's not, like, it's not gone, like, real old news or whatever, but there's not, like, in promotion of some new movie.

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:36.080
Yeah, but all things considered, it's this being, like, ending in 1988 is, like, that's, like, pretty good compared to, like, half the other games.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:37.600
Like, that's just happening right now.

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:41.260
Like, we've had games that were, like, from properties from, like, the 60s only.

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:43.580
Yeah, this isn't, like, three stooges in Jaws.

00:24:43.620 --> 00:24:49.260
Like, this is much more in vogue than I expected it to be.

00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:53.020
I didn't realize that it was up to 1988, actually.

00:24:53.020 --> 00:24:53.880
That's pretty recent.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:57.280
Yeah, you think about 71 to 88, but it's five films.

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:59.580
So it's, like, they really knew how to draw them out back then.

00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:07.200
And going through, probably, like, I'm just going to skip through, like, most of the rest of this game.

00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:10.600
Harry's arsenal expands.

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:12.880
Obviously, we get more enemies and everything.

00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.840
We go to two different stages.

00:25:14.840 --> 00:25:20.060
We have the docks, and we have Alcatraz Island as our final stages.

00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:23.000
So there's only three stages, and the game does make that clear.

00:25:23.220 --> 00:25:25.940
They just don't make it clear, like, how big those things are.

00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:28.460
They make it seem like it's just level one, level two, level three.

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:30.760
But they ask you for that when you start the game.

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:34.200
Do you want to, like, do you put in a password for level two or three?

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:35.900
And you're kind of like, only three levels?

00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:37.020
Like, that's kind of interesting.

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:39.780
Level one is pretty huge, though.

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:46.280
But, like, you think that with the whole sort of, I guess, the big city.

00:25:46.480 --> 00:25:49.260
Like, the big, like, complex city arrangement.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.100
You expect that to be the norm.

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:53.500
And it really isn't that.

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:57.480
Like, the city is only, like, half of level one.

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:06.240
And then the other, I want to say, like, 55% of it is in the sewers, which is much less fun and much less interesting.

00:26:06.540 --> 00:26:13.260
I mean, not to say that the city was perfect execution on everything.

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:18.360
But at least, like, it felt more like an interesting environment to explore.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:21.680
Whereas the sewers are just, you know, another video game sewer.

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:28.660
I don't know. But does it ever feel like the stakes are getting larger as the game goes on?

00:26:28.660 --> 00:26:32.960
As you're taking down this larger super gang that we discussed?

00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:36.820
You do have access to some pretty cool stuff as the game goes on.

00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:39.500
You get the, there's rockets.

00:26:39.500 --> 00:26:40.600
There's a harpoon.

00:26:42.680 --> 00:26:44.220
And the RC cars.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:48.220
Yes, the RC cars.

00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:49.180
No better way to raise the stakes.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:51.860
Yeah. The RC explosive cars, keep in mind.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.440
It's like, did he go to queue for those?

00:26:53.560 --> 00:27:00.940
Like, what's happening? Health, though, is refilled by eating hot dogs that you find on the streets.

00:27:00.940 --> 00:27:06.980
And I hope nobody, and I mean nobody, put ketchup on those hot dogs.

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:10.480
Okay. Is this, are you trying to make a statement right now?

00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:14.080
Like, it's a reference from the film.

00:27:14.480 --> 00:27:15.680
Wait, from the first one?

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:18.140
I don't actually know if it's from the first one.

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:22.980
I can't say. I just know he does indeed eat a hot dog in the first movie.

00:27:23.460 --> 00:27:28.620
He, he, he has, there are hot dog references, but the one I think specifically that they're

00:27:28.620 --> 00:27:32.500
going for is he sees another police officer eating a hot dog.

00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:38.780
And he says, nobody, and I mean nobody, puts ketchup on a hot dog.

00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:43.220
Well, that's one thing that me and Clint disagree because.

00:27:43.600 --> 00:27:47.100
It's also, yeah. I mean, cause like I've, I've really never heard of ketchup on a hot dog.

00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:49.280
It is a weird thing. What are you talking about?

00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:52.460
Ketchup on a hot dog?

00:27:53.120 --> 00:27:54.660
I've never heard of ketchup on a hot dog.

00:27:55.200 --> 00:27:57.880
You're just, you're really, you really just fuck with me right now.

00:27:58.020 --> 00:27:59.520
Yeah, of course I'm fucking with you.

00:28:00.180 --> 00:28:02.080
Of course I've heard of ketchup on a hot dog.

00:28:03.020 --> 00:28:08.740
Um, but I have heard the opinion only mustard on a hot dog, which I think is a, is a little

00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:10.580
like a little bit of a hot take.

00:28:10.740 --> 00:28:14.560
And personally, if you only got, if you only got mustard, I'm okay with having only mustard

00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:16.040
on a hot dog. Uh, yeah, sure.

00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:18.440
I like it, but also there's nothing wrong with ketchup on a hot dog.

00:28:18.440 --> 00:28:22.660
I am sorry to say that it took me 32 years.

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:24.380
I am 33 years old.

00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:31.100
So I found out last year that ketchup is like the lowest of the lows on a hot dog.

00:28:31.280 --> 00:28:33.080
Like there are so many better things.

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:35.840
Like I will, I almost never put ketchup on a hot dog now.

00:28:35.940 --> 00:28:38.580
It's like, I, if there's only ketchup, I'll do it.

00:28:39.020 --> 00:28:42.160
But I have like so many other options before I go to.

00:28:42.260 --> 00:28:45.820
Well, yeah, but most of the other things I put on it go with ketchup.

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:47.720
I would put ketchup, mustard.

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:53.880
You know, I would put Cram Rangoon on there before I put, before I put ketchup back on.

00:28:54.300 --> 00:28:56.600
Oh, just like cream cheese on your hot dog.

00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:58.400
No, I never said cream cheese.

00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:01.200
Get the Cram Rangoon has cream cheese in it.

00:29:01.380 --> 00:29:02.660
Right, but there's, but there's other ingredients.

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:04.640
You said it, Mike. Right, that's true.

00:29:04.760 --> 00:29:06.240
But there's other ingredients. It wasn't implied.

00:29:06.580 --> 00:29:07.640
There still is cream cheese on your hot dog.

00:29:07.860 --> 00:29:09.880
You know, what's actually a really good thing for a hot dog?

00:29:10.020 --> 00:29:14.360
And you guys are going to probably say that this isn't a problem and you're just going

00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:18.420
to agree. So I don't know why I'm making it a big deal, but it's really, really good.

00:29:18.440 --> 00:29:23.660
It's really good to put a sliced pickle in the hot dog bun with your hot dog.

00:29:23.660 --> 00:29:26.000
Yeah, welcome to the 21st century, Mike.

00:29:26.040 --> 00:29:29.320
Yeah, that's like, it's just as normal as putting ketchup on a hot dog.

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:32.020
I didn't know about like the sliced pickle.

00:29:32.140 --> 00:29:35.960
I know about relish, obviously, but I'm talking about like just a nice sliced pickle.

00:29:35.960 --> 00:29:38.440
Yeah. Do you guys know of Piccolilly or is it?

00:29:38.520 --> 00:29:42.760
Well, Sean, you might. It's like a Western New York thing, maybe, or maybe it's outside of Western New York, but

00:29:42.760 --> 00:29:44.200
I feel like it might be a local thing.

00:29:44.440 --> 00:29:45.560
I don't know about Piccolilly.

00:29:45.960 --> 00:29:50.200
It's like a hot, pickly, peppery relish, but it's just the perfect combination.

00:29:50.340 --> 00:29:51.680
That's my favorite thing on a hot dog.

